[2026-11-24T22:13:57Z] note: setup: 11 Select Sector SPDRs (XLB XLC XLE XLF XLI XLK XLP XLRE XLU XLV XLY), Yahoo daily adjusted, data 1998-12-22..2026-11-23 (XLRE 2015-10, XLC 2018-06). IS 2000-07-01..2016-01-01, OOS 2016-01-01..2026-11-23 (end frozen). One portfolio, 10,000 USD, weights 1/N per eligible sector, fee 0.05%/side, slippage 0.03%/fill.
[2026-11-24T22:13:57Z] note: assumptions: (1) point-in-time universe: an ETF counts toward breadth once listed and SMA(n) exists (spec: no backfill before listing); (2) cash at 0% yield, the spec's labeled conservative scenario; (3) whole sleeve with target weights, no risk_fraction sizing (user's 100%-equity choice for library specs); (4) adjusted closes used for signals and fills; (5) monthly resize without tolerance band (spec has none); (6) one trade = one holding from first buy to full close, trims/additions included in its P&L.
[2026-11-24T22:13:57Z] note: backtest.py adapted from template: strategy block (CONFIG/PARAMS/SPACE, eligibility close>SMA(n)) plus machinery change: run() calls a new _simulate_portfolio instead of per-symbol _simulate, because breadth B is cross-sectional and weights are B/count(eligible)=1/N. Implements month-end decisions on complete months, next-open fills, sells before buys, cash-scaled buys, hard stop from weighted-average cost never loosened, gap stops at open, max_candles from entry bar, no re-entry on the exit bar, skip rebalance on a missing member bar. load_bars/metrics unchanged.
[2026-11-24T22:13:57Z] note: sanity check: defaults (n200, stop15, max252) IS 6.07%/yr, 163 trades, DD -19.3%, PF 2.86, win 52%; OOS 7.48%/yr, 154 trades, DD -14.5%. Verified: all entries on a month's first bar, max_bars exits at exactly 252 bars, stops fill at E*0.85 or at a gap-down open (XLV 2002-07-11), XLE close 24.16 > SMA200 21.21 on 2008-05-30 recomputed independently, equity end matches summed trade P&L (diff = exit costs of open positions). ~0.36 s per backtest.
[2026-11-24T22:13:57Z] note: plan: base run only on the 11-ETF universe. Screening, broad basket and per-symbol runs skipped: breadth is cross-sectional, a single-symbol run degenerates into a different strategy (SMA filter + stop), and swapping in other universes would change the spec. Grid 7,182 sets fits the budget, so the optimizer should search it exhaustively.
